    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our primary catalyst; despite a marginal park factor, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Lambert and a slow delivery that elevates his stolen base potential significantly. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a massive outing against Kay, where he leverages a strong park factor and a 16% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s projected xERA to anchor the utility spot. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) also merits attention as a Tier-1 play, benefiting from Lugo\u2019s higher xERA and a potent dynamic platoon advantage.\n\nConversely, we are exercising caution with the bottom of our roster as the league\u2019s strict 5x5 Roto constraints reward efficiency. **Miguel Vargas** (43.79) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; while his xwOBA of .401 is elite, he was bumped for players with higher situational leverage in the batting order. We are also wary of the risks surrounding **Liam Hicks** (41.57) and **Coby Mayo** (44.68), both of whom are hovering near our efficiency floor. The matchup against Henderson (3.17 xERA) puts **Liam Hicks** at risk of a quiet day, and while **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same soft matchup as **Gunnar Henderson**, his spot at the bottom of the order suppresses his scoring ceiling. \n\nStrategic notes for today include monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 70.50 reflects a strong combination of an elite batting position and a favorable matchup against Quantrill. His 19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s high xERA is the most significant situational tailwind in the lineup. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but we remain vigilant regarding the confirmed lineups for those currently marked as \"Pending\" to ensure our stolen base threats, specifically those with favorable platoon splits like **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci**, maintain their projected optimal spots.",
